WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.502
-You have pulled off -- I don'
think people quite appreciat

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
the coup that you pulled off
with this show "Tommy"

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:09.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it is about
an L.A. police chief.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet it is filmed
in New York City.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Which is insane.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Sometimes they will shoot

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
Vancouver and try to make that
look like New York

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's
cheaper in Vancouver.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nothing is more expensive
than New York City.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, here they are
pretending

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make it look
like Los Angeles.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:27.861 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.929 line:92%
-You know, for it to be a coup

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to have some sort of
volition, I think.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.134
-Yeah, that's true, yeah.
-'Cause I didn't with this

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
I read it, and I thought,
"Oh, this is so good,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.737 line:92%
but it's in L.A. Oh, well.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.671 line:92%
And that was the end of it

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my agent
came back and said,

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, what if they shot i
in New York?"

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.144 line:92%
I thought he was making a joke

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
But apparently he wasn't.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.746 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-We have our palm trees

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we stick them
in front of each location.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it works.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.685 size:84% position:42%
-I mean, we've only had
one episode air so far.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not a ton of comments.
-That's true.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.522 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"That's not L.A."

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll see.
We'll see how it goes.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.360 line:92%
-Have there been moments -

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, there's different
weather patterns.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Indeed.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, on my phone,
I have us shooting

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.502 line:92%
exterior scenes in a squall.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.572
Remember that night where
there was those crazy snowstorms

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.973 line:92%
around November or something

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was insane,
really insane.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:18.578
The poor guys would come out
and wipe all the cars down

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.979 line:92%
"Roll camera, roll camera!

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyway.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.415 line:92%
I don't know if it has legs.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We'll see.
-We'll see. We shall see.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.119 line:92%
-How do you -- you have been -

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
You appeared in shows with
police before.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.521 line:92%
You've never played -- I believe

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the first time you'v
played a police officer?

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.758 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, it is, I guess.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:35.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
I played an E.M.T.
and a prison warden.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they all carry thing
to hit people with.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.900 line:92%
-Do you think you, in general,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
would have made
a good police officer?

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.171 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I do. I do, actually.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.039 line:92%
It's an interesting question

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm bossy.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm type-A. I like to tel
people what to do.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.413
-That all sounds pretty much
right in the job description

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pretty much, yeah.
-What about the uniform?

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you enjoy that?
-Hideous.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.218 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I got to to say.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
I like the authenticity piece,

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the uniforms
are made out of

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:05.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
some plastic amalgamation,
something.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Horrible.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:07.760 line:92%
They're so uncomfortable.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I mean, I have
a whole, new -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what it takes for m
to have a respect for the cops

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're able to wear
these things all day.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just horrible.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, a very unique
costume over years

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.575 line:92%
you did was Carmela Soprano.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you find over time
that you enjoyed that style?

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you go,
"I like Carmela's style"?

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.782 size:81% position:41%
Or were you very happy
to say goodbye to it?

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Never happened. Not once.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Even at the end of
all the years of shooting,

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll often say,
"Take a look at your wardrobe.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want to take
any of it home?"

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "No."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.627 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-That is a clean break.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is good.
I need to really separate.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.033
It's always such a delight
to have you on the show.

